oyees are required to contribute 5% of their gross salary, while Penn State contributes 9.29% of the employee's gross salary. The plan may accept rollovers from other employer's plans, which can increase the maximum loan amount. In terms of taxes, Pennsylvania is tax-friendly towards retirees, does not tax social security income or withdrawals from retirement accounts. Both public and private pension income are not taxed.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}", "role": "user"}], "model": "unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF", "seed": 7078188, "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1}
