e shell of valence electrons, allowing it to form compounds with an oxidation number of -1.\\n* Gold is a heavy metal with a density of 19.3 g/cm\\u00b3.\\n* One gram of gold can be hammered out into a thin sheet of gold covering a meter in area, and is translucent with a greenish-blue color.\\n* Gold is malleable and ductile, meaning it can be easily beaten into thin sheets and drawn out into wires without breaking.\\n* Gold is a soft metal and is typically alloyed with other metals to increase its strength.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}", "role": "user"}], "model": "unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF", "seed": 7078188, "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1}
